He also compares the average business owner with the average employee. The transcript gives the rough comparison as 58 to 55 and says that the employee makes about $\$3{,}000$ to $\$4{,}000$ more. The safest notation keeps the unit cautious: $\bar I_{\hbox{employee}}
  -
  \bar I_{\hbox{business owner}}
  \approx
  \$3{,}000\hbox{ to }\$4{,}000.$ The numerical precision is not the point. The point is that ownership alone is not wealth. The base rates make entrepreneurship a conditional choice, not an identity.

