The crucial contrast is between incremental improvement and real scale. Mitt says a CRM, a new technology, or one smart hire may improve the business by $10\%$ or $20\%$, but it will not by itself double, triple, or quadruple revenue: $\Delta_{\hbox{tool}}
  \approx 10\%\hbox{ to }20\%,
  \qquad
  \Delta_{\hbox{scale}}
  \in
  \{2\times,3\times,4\times,\ldots\}.$

